    {
      "type": "patchouli:spotlight",
      "item": "theoreticalsciences:penrose_ergosphere",
      "title": "Penrose Ergosphere Generator",
      "text": "Extracts the rotational energy of a spinning black hole via the $(thing)Penrose process$(). My first real power from a singularity.$(br2)Generates power.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 3$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "$(thing)Made on the Extreme Assembly Table$() (it is also a crafting table). The recipe pages at the end of this entry - and JEI - show the pattern."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Penrose, 1969: around a rotating hole lies the $(thing)ergosphere$(), where spacetime itself is dragged so hard nothing can stand still. Split a particle there, drop one half onto a negative-energy orbit, and the other escapes with more energy than you sent in. The hole spins down to pay for it."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Running figures: a $(item)Micro Singularity$() burns for twenty minutes at 65,536 FE/t. Energy leaves through the controller and any $(item)Interface Port$()."
    },
